{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8b5f0e0c-996b-536d-8e89-6f6cec7d7b81",
    "name": "Fortis API - Fortis staff",
    "description": "Every Fortis staff (platform) route of the backend (prefix `/api/v1`): staff sign-in and passwords, the business directory, provisioning, branch creation, the public business request form, and staff invitations. Business-user routes are in **Fortis API - Business users**.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Start the API with its services: `npm run dev:up`, `npm run db:migrate`, `npm run start:dev`.\n2. Set `baseUrl` (default `http://localhost:3000/api/v1`), `platformEmail` and `platformPassword`.\n3. Run **01 Sign in and session > Login**. It stores the staff tokens.\n\nThe first (bootstrap) staff account is created directly in the database by an operator; there is no API for it. Emailed tokens (password reset, staff invitations) must be copied from the email; locally they are in the Mailpit inbox.\n\n## Authentication and checks\n\nCollection auth is `Bearer {{platformAccessToken}}`; public routes override it with *No Auth*. Every request checks the `X-Request-Id` header and, for errors, the `{ statusCode, error, message, requestId }` body. Each request adds its own checks and stores the ids later requests need.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{platformAccessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Shared checks for every request in this collection.",
          "pm.test('carries a request id', () => {",
          "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Request-Id')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
          "});",
          "if (pm.response.code >= 400) {",
          "  pm.test('error body has statusCode and message', () => {",
          "    const body = pm.response.json();",
          "    pm.expect(body.statusCode).to.eql(pm.response.code);",
          "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('message');",
          "  });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
